    "body": "@kevinSuttle CSS variables do not interact with HTML color syntax, it's true. That's kind of an interesting suggestion in general, and I wonder if @tabatkins has thoughts; on the surface it seems hard to implement in a performant way. Probably the best route forward for harmonizing CSS and theme-color is to just introduce an equivalent CSS construct, as was proposed in https://github.com/whatwg/meta-theme-color/issues/5. But then again there were good arguments against putting it in CSS there.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
