    "body": "Sorry, I forgot to make the PR! I'm super busy now.\n\nSince the last discussion (which is still valid), the FT app has added one more twist: it now _dynamically_ changes theme color `<meta>` to match the theme of the currently displayed section:\n\n<img src=https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/72159/18769904/0a70ae76-8129-11e6-96ce-e51317bfc4a7.png  width=200> <img src=https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/72159/18769903/0a7077f8-8129-11e6-94cf-467d0614f3cc.jpg width=200> <img src=https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/72159/18769905/0a70fa02-8129-11e6-947b-c4665bcb03e9.jpg  width=200>\n- it looks _really nice_ in Chrome! It was even nicer in older Chrome version with tabs mixed with system apps retaining the color for the app's titlebar (latest Chrome has generic gray for app titlebar 😭 )\n- Fortunately, Chrome-powered PWA prefers theme from `<meta>` over [JSON metatags](https://app.ft.com/metatags.json), so we get nice dynamic app titlebar color there :)\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
