    "body": "@domenic @tabatkins I think that careful consideration needs to take place to reduce the duplication and single-source theme colors, while exposing them to CSS, HTML, AMP, and JS as much as possible. cc: @cramforce\n\n**main.css**\n\n``` css\n:root {\n    --ThemeColor: #3f51b5\n}\n```\n\n**manifest.json**\n\n``` json\n{\n  \"theme_color\": \"#3f51b5\",\n  \"background_color\": \"#3f51b5\",\n}\n```\n\n**index.html**\n\n``` html\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#3f51b5\">\n<meta name=\"msapplication-TileColor\" content=\"#3f51b5\">\n```\n\n**index.amp.html ?**\n\n``` html\n  <noscript><style amp-boilerplate></style></noscript>\n```\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
